7. Benefits of Collaborative Software Development
• Improved software quality: Contributions from different people can identify and correct missing or unclear information.
• Knowledge sharing: Students and developers learn from one another and gain practical experience.
• Better documentation: Clear instructions make the software easier for new users to understand.
• Community participation: Pull Requests allow contributors to work transparently while maintainers review and manage changes.
• Continuous improvement: The project can be updated regularly as user needs and software features change.
8. Conclusion
The student can improve the Library Management System by adding clear documentation for issuing and returning books. GitHub supports this contribution through forking, editing, committing, and submitting a Pull Request. After the maintainers review and merge the changes, the improved guide becomes available to all users of the project. This process demonstrates how open-source software engineering encourages collaboration, learning, and continuous improvement.
